eligibility_summary:
To be eligible, applicants must:
Be currently enrolled in second year or above of an undergraduate program in the Faculty of Science or a science-related discipline at UNSW or another Australian or New Zealand University.
Be able to be engaged in a project on a full-time basis (35 hours/week for six weeks during normal working hours unless advised otherwise by the supervisor);
Projects must be focused on research-based activities (administration tasks are not regarded as research) and should be completed by the end of February;
Each successful candidate can hold only ONE such scholarship at a time;
Students who were previously awarded a UNSW Science Vacation Research Scholarship are not eligible to apply.

The recipient must be:
Undertaking / commencing full-time undergraduate study with the Faculty of Built Environment, and;
Selected for international course at the Hong Kong or Shanghai Global Studio in 2026.

To be eligible for nomination you must:
Be an Australian citizen;
Not hold citizenship or permanent residency for your proposed host location;
Be enrolled in an undergraduate degree at UNSW and receive credit for the study (student exchange) component of the NCP Scholarship Program;
Be between 18 and 30 years of age (inclusive) for non-Indigenous applicants, or between 18 and 35 years of age (inclusive) for Indigenous applicants as of 1 January 2027;
Hold a minimum 70% WAM at the time of application;
Undertake your exchange in 2027. You need to apply for UNSW Exchange by 29 April 2026 for exchange in Term 1 2027 or 17 September 2026 for exchange in Term 3 2027;
Receive credit from your student exchange towards your UNSW degree;
Have remaining units of credit in your UNSW degree program after completing the NCP scholarship program;
Not have previously received an NCP Scholarship;
Not be an employee of the DFAT branch that administers NCP.
Before applying, please ensure you:
Read the NCP Scholarship Program guidelines and Advice to Applicants.
As the 2027 guidelines have not yet been released, refer to the
2026 guidelines and advice
.
Review the
Applying for Exchange Moodle tutorial
and understand the application process and deadlines.

